From: kalaga <kalaga@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:58:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 68/76] Shaders: a thread group's first thread always sets up
 its shared memory

A compute program that sets its LDS up from the group's first thread
alone (constants to constant addresses under v_cmpx_eq_u32 exec, 0,
<thread place>) skipped that set-up when that thread had left already.
On the console the group then starts from the neighbouring tile's sane
values; on a PC card from anything. In the water's tiled light
(water_shading:CS_TransmissionVolumetrics_Tiled) 71 of 124 tiles whose
first pixel was not water wrote nothing: dark slabs on the water along
the horizon and beside rocks, plants and hulls. The first thread now
always does it (VICTORY_LDS_FIRST_INIT=0: as the console); part of the
shader cache fingerprint. Bounded by the program's own LDS size here.

From readmet3xt-lab/foxhound (lower.rs first_thread_init, 2026-11-27).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6tkVHCftUUQbGm5NirGaG
